                <pb facs="0557" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C1199/248: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-11-24T15:00:00+01:00">November 24,
                            1936—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 26—7:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>478. Department’s telegram 146, November 23, noon. The Council in its session
                    convening January 18 will appoint the entire membership of the Economic
                    Committee, thus the reappointment of present incumbents is not automatic.</p>
                <p>Stoppani states that provided he be concurrently informed that the individual
                    concerned would accept, the American whose appointment is desired could be named
                    to him as late as January 7. This is, however, the extreme date which would
                    permit him to take necessary steps. Should a name or names merely be “suggested”
                    to him, a much earlier date would be possible in order to ascertain willingness
                    to accept, etc.</p>
                <p>This is naturally a practical expression of the situation; I appreciate that
                    technically the Department’s action is limited to suggestions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
